  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "Security update for gimp",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "Summary"
    },
    {
      "Text": "This update for gimp fixes the following issues:\n\nChanges in gimp:\n\n- CVE-2026-78465: 32-bit integer overflow in PCX image memory calculations can cause undersized heap allocations (bsc#1277378)\n- CVE-2026-78475: unbounded variable-length stack allocations in the PIX loader can cause stack exhaustion crashes and stack memory disclosures (bsc#1277380)\n- CVE-2026-80101: independent header field validation in the XWD loader can cause heap out-of-bounds reads (bsc#1276911)\n",
      "Title": "Details",
      "Type": "General"
    },
